--- KEY-02: the article `the` references an existing variable ---
a number called cupboard is 91.
Set the cupboard to 51032.
If the cupboard is not 51032 then, Print "ASSERT KEY-02: expected 51032 got {the cupboard}", Exit 95. Print the cupboard.

--- the same leaf, nested ---
  a number called cupboard is 91,
  Set the cupboard to 51032,
  If the cupboard is not 51032 then, Print "ASSERT KEY-02: expected 51032 got {the cupboard}", Exit 95. Print the cupboard.

--- KEY-04: Set/Create declaration forms ---
Set a number called 'the inbox' to 6979343254000059.
If 'the inbox' is not 6979343254000059 then, Print "ASSERT KEY-04: expected 6979343254000059 got {'the inbox'}", Exit 95. Print 'the inbox'.
Create a text called 'the sketchpad' to "the returned thing the outturn the tally".
If 'the sketchpad' is not "the returned thing the outturn the tally" then, Print "ASSERT KEY-04: expected the returned thing the outturn the tally got {'the sketchpad'}", Exit 95. Print 'the sketchpad'.
Create a number called 'the waybill'.
If 'the waybill' is not 0 then, Print "ASSERT KEY-04: expected 0 got {'the waybill'}", Exit 95. Print 'the waybill'.

--- KEY-11: Decrement, bare and `the`-prefixed ---
a number called 'the dispatch note' is 6.
Decrement 'the dispatch note'.
Decrement the 'the dispatch note'.
If 'the dispatch note' is not 4 then, Print "ASSERT KEY-11: expected 4 got {'the dispatch note'}", Exit 95. Print 'the dispatch note'.

--- KEY-44, KEY-45: the `and` subject-list terminator ---
a boolean called scratch is true.
a boolean called 'the sketchpad' is true.
a boolean called 'the tray' is true.
a boolean called 'the postbag' is false.
If scratch, 'the sketchpad', and 'the tray' are true then, Set 'the postbag' to true.
If 'the postbag' is false then, Print "ASSERT KEY-44: expected 1 got {'the postbag'}", Exit 95. Print 'the postbag'.
a boolean called 'the pallet' is false.
If scratch, 'the sketchpad', and 'the tray' are not false then, Set 'the pallet' to true.
If 'the pallet' is false then, Print "ASSERT KEY-44: expected 1 got {'the pallet'}", Exit 95. Print 'the pallet'.
a number called pantry is 2147483648.
a number called 'the inbox' is 2147483648.
a number called 'the greeting' is 0.
a boolean called 'the shipping label' is false.
If pantry, 'the inbox', and 'the greeting' are 2147483648 then, Set 'the shipping label' to true.
If 'the shipping label' then, Print "ASSERT KEY-45: expected 0 got {'the shipping label'}", Exit 95. Print 'the shipping label'.

--- KEY-49, KEY-50: message/string as reserved aliases of text ---
a message called 'the register' is "the tally taken".
a string called 'the sketchpad' is "the pouch the reading taken".
If 'the register's type is not "Text (static)" then, Print "ASSERT KEY-49: expected Text (static) got {'the register's type}", Exit 95. Print 'the register's type.
If 'the register' is not "the tally taken" then, Print "ASSERT KEY-49: expected the tally taken got {'the register'}", Exit 95. Print 'the register'.
If 'the sketchpad's type is not "Text (static)" then, Print "ASSERT KEY-50: expected Text (static) got {'the sketchpad's type}", Exit 95. Print 'the sketchpad's type.
If 'the sketchpad' is not "the pouch the reading taken" then, Print "ASSERT KEY-50: expected the pouch the reading taken got {'the sketchpad'}", Exit 95. Print 'the sketchpad'.

--- KEY-53, KEY-54: length as a contextual keyword ---
a number called length is 0.
a buffer called 'the waybill' is 34 bytes in size.
append "" to 'the waybill'.
If 'the waybill's length is not 'the waybill's size then, Print "ASSERT KEY-54: expected {'the waybill's size} got {'the waybill's length}", Exit 95. Print 'the waybill's length.
a list called 'the envelope' is [5, 8762, 3986231888985390].
If 'the envelope's length is not 'the envelope's size then, Print "ASSERT KEY-54: expected {'the envelope's size} got {'the envelope's length}", Exit 95. Print 'the envelope's length.
If length is not 0 then, Print "ASSERT KEY-53: expected 0 got {length}", Exit 95. Print length.

--- KEY-73: version as a contextual keyword (ordinary-identifier half) ---
a number called version is 369199.
If version is not 369199 then, Print "ASSERT KEY-73: expected 369199 got {version}", Exit 95. Print version.

